From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:18:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] config: enable ZRAM_WRITEBACK for the ExtM probe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Enable CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK so system_perf_init can set a backing device
and system_server can read /sys/block/zram0/backing_dev. This is the A
probe for Xiaomi ExtM; if PerfInit still skips ExtM, the startup gate is
elsewhere.

Origin: 本地配置（ExtM A 探针）
Upstream-Status: Not-Applicable
KABI: none
Depends-On: none
Tested-On: yudi 5.10.272, 2026-10-29

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index 7250349a5..2b7b21253 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -901,3 +901,6 @@ CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_ADIOS=y
 
 # Phase 10.7: power-efficient unbound workqueues (gray test).
 CONFIG_WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT_DEFAULT=y
+
+# Phase 10.8: zram writeback for the ExtM probe.
+CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK=y
-- 
2.34.1

